      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can report the issue to your local council's street lighting department. They'll likely have a system in place to track the repair, and you can expect a response within a few days. You might want to check their website or social media for updates, as some councils have online portals for reporting issues and tracking progress. Just be prepared to provide as much detail as possible, like the exact location and the time of day the flickering occurs. \n\nYou can also try contacting the council's customer service department directly, and they'll likely direct you to the right person to report the issue. They might even have a \"report a streetlight\" form on their website that you can fill out online. \n\nIt's a bit like a lost treasure hunt, but instead of a chest filled with gold, you're searching for a functioning streetlamp. But don't worry, with persistence and the right resources, you'll be able to track down the issue and get the lamp fixed.",
